WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.756
Then every vault gets six checks from
Learn's Key Vault recommendations:

2
00:00:04.756 --> 00:00:08.442
role-based access, not access
policies; purge protection;

3
00:00:08.442 --> 00:00:13.227
a firewall whose default is deny; public
network access, which is a warning;

4
00:00:13.227 --> 00:00:18.325
an approved private endpoint; and audit
events sent to the platform workspace.

5
00:00:18.325 --> 00:00:22.936
A vault has the full posture when it
has role-based access, purge protection,

6
00:00:22.936 --> 00:00:25.688
an approved private
endpoint and audit logs:

7
00:00:25.688 --> 00:00:28.737
the four parts of the
guide's vault-posture metric.

8
00:00:28.737 --> 00:00:32.635
Key rotation policies are read
through the vault's own data plane,

9
00:00:32.635 --> 00:00:34.150
which the kit doesn't call.

10
00:00:34.150 --> 00:00:36.860
Lab 2 reads one with the guide's command.
